  "verified_claims": [
    "PostgreSQL 17 commits manifest, Pending TaskRun, and reserved stream in one transaction; API death before manifest commit rolls back all three.",
    "Exact client/API response loss, 16 concurrent exact callers, and request drift preserve one TaskRun and one stream.",
    "Existing Running execution refuses with RECOVERY_NOT_READY through normal TaskRun state API; no unsafe reconstruction is exposed.",
    "Hard limits of 128 manifests, 1 MiB canonical metadata per FlowRun, 64 KiB per canonical manifest, and 32 KiB parameters reject before partial creation.",
    "The selected topology has one source root and no fan-out; unsupported topology fails before mutation.",
    "Normal CoreFlowPolicy cancellation permits whole-flow release; lookup retains a RELEASED witness and execution replay returns REPLAY_HORIZON_EXPIRED.",
    "PostgreSQL and SQLite paired migrations/DDL parity pass; SQLite runtime capability remains fail-closed before data-plane writes.",
    "Client/server schema and sync/async method parity, stripped client package, existing native stream contracts, TaskRun API, OpenAPI/UI generation, hooks, types and public completeness pass on the same source map."
